**Definition 5.1 (the four exposures and their common context).** At
the completed acquisition cut fix the genuine context of Section 1,
the original design and initial table, the fixed startup schedule and
the complete current geometry/table. On later cuts also fix the
actually maintained growth provenance distinguishing old commissioned
edges from known birth edges. These are earned or supplied actual
context; they do not include $T,x,w$ or free hidden advice. Expose:

| Expression | Independently specified content |
| --- | --- |
| Literal Space | The current material incidence, actual signed coefficients/diagonals and actual field in persistent material addresses; no acquisition journal |
| Time | The actually performed pre-growth Hold, inherited splits and fixed free/pulse call window, operands, literal returned scalars and completion order/frames; no unobserved preparation word |
| Boundary | Current terminal impulse response and current passive free germ, finitely encoded as $\mathcal B(A,w)=((CA^rB)_{0\le r\le2M-1},(CA^rw)_{0\le r\le M-1})$ |
| Memory | The actually retained numerical law/current-field predictor and mutable code/table/parser, together with genuine separately retained reference, grants, backing and any explicitly retained archive |

Boundary has an experimental terminal meaning before any inverse is
specified. At this cut it is a paid computed export of the acquired
predictor. Future-time germ entries are predicted values, not newly
performed Reads. A requested new physical observation window has its
own Ticks, changed endpoint, Reads, holds and records. Time's numerical
content is the stated finite measured window, with its fixed completed
phases; it is not arbitrary wall time or a copy of the whole source
history. Memory need not retain the raw calibration tape for current
prediction. A numerical inverse cannot reconstruct identity, authority,
custody, authentic bytes or occurrence of an execution.

